  "notes": "Migos' tour DJ turned in-house producer, and the research is unambiguous about where the interest lives: \"hats are the focus\" and drum-sound selection is the stated priority. So this model puts almost all of its budget in one block. `hihat.fillDensity` 0.75 is the highest in this batch, `fill.prob` 0.8 with 32nd/64th subdivisions and nine notes carries the layered rolls, and `pitchBendProb` 0.45 with `swellProb` 0.35 is the pitched hat variation the paragraph names — nothing else on this bench bends hats that hard. Harmony is deliberately the opposite: \"the hunt is for unusual timbres rather than unusual harmony\", so `impliedByRiff` is set over static vamps and two-chord beds and the melody is a small pitch set sitting very high (78–102) over a root-only low voice. The ad-lib-driven answer patterns are `countermelody.styles` led by `answer_lick`. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium. The inferred parameters are the melodic register bounds and `kick.densityPerBar`; the paragraph gives the hat grammar in detail but the pitch material only as \"small pitch sets\". ⚠ The i–VI and i–VII families are the research's \"two-chord beds\"; the chord part's variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` and three harmonic rhythms rather than from added progressions.",
